virglrenderer: Venus frees name objects of their own pool, once

What: vkFreeCommandBuffers and vkFreeDescriptorSets check every handle before any is
freed: each command buffer or set belongs to the pool the call names and is named
once (a stamp per call marks them, no allocation; NULL handles stay allowed).
Pooled objects keep their pool for this. A refusal ends the app's context (frees
have no answer).
Why: the driver frees each handle it is handed into the pool it is told. KosmicKrisp
destroyed a set named twice twice (SIGSEGV in kk_FreeDescriptorSets); Mesa's runtime
put a command buffer of another pool into this pool's list (SIGSEGV when that pool
was destroyed); KosmicKrisp's descriptor pool took over another pool's memory range,
which its next set then used, so descriptor writes landed outside the pool's buffer.
Probed on the M4 (Apple9) with KosmicKrisp and MoltenVK.
Upstream: OmacVM policy (VUIDs vkFreeCommandBuffers-pCommandBuffers-parent,
vkFreeDescriptorSets-pDescriptorSets-parent and -00310).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (the f- cases, also under libgmalloc).

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.c b/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.c
index 1525903..eb3a16f 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.c
@@ -642,7 +642,8 @@ vkr_dispatch_vkFreeCommandBuffers(struct vn_dispatch_context *dispatch,
       return;
    }
 
-   vkr_command_buffer_destroy_driver_handles(ctx, args, &free_list);
+   if (!vkr_command_buffer_destroy_driver_handles(ctx, args, &free_list))
+      return;
    vkr_context_remove_objects(ctx, &free_list);
 }
 
diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.h b/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.h
index 3aa221d..96101d4 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.h
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_command_buffer.h
@@ -51,6 +51,10 @@ struct vkr_command_buffer {
    struct vkr_object base;
 
    struct vkr_device *device;
+   /* OmacVM (virgl-venus-pool-frees.patch): its pool, and the stamp of the last free call
+    * that named it */
+   struct vkr_command_pool *pool;
+   uint64_t free_stamp;
    /* OmacVM (virgl-venus-command-limits.patch): only a primary executes secondaries */
    VkCommandBufferLevel level;
    struct vkr_cmd_state state;
diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_descriptor_set.c b/src/venus/vkr_descriptor_set.c
